        "met_days": 17.01,
        "type": "edl_or_oi",
        "label": "Lunar orbit insertion + MIP release",
        "description": "2008-11-08. Captured into a 100-km polar lunar orbit. Released the Moon Impact Probe on 2008-11-14, which hard-landed at Shackleton crater near the south pole — making India the 5th national space agency to reach the lunar surface. Mission ended 2009-08-29 (10 months) when the spacecraft's thermal control failed. NASA's M³ data was later analysed to discover lunar surface water at >40 ppm."
      }
